faqs:
- q: Do you unpack for us?
  a: Yes, from Silver Comfort at {silver}, which includes unpacking and set-up at the new home. Gold Prestige at {gold} adds white-glove unpacking and styling. Bronze Essentials includes packing, an insured removal, furniture reassembly and a light clean, but not unpacking.
- q: What does a settling-in service include?
  a: It depends on the package. Unpacking and set-up come with Silver Comfort. Platinum Bespoke at {platinum} adds a lifestyle concierge for three months after the move, helping with new-area orientation and introductions to local services and community groups.
- q: What is white-glove unpacking?
  a: It is the unpacking and styling included in Gold Prestige, on top of everything in Silver Comfort.
- q: Can you set up furniture and a first-night room?
  a: Furniture is reassembled from Bronze Essentials, and with unpacking from Silver Comfort the new home is set up so the bed, kitchen and bathroom are ready. We also suggest a clearly labelled first-night box.
- q: How long does settling in take?
  a: That varies from person to person, so we do not put a number on it. Platinum Bespoke includes three months of concierge support after the move, and our <a href="/blog/settling-in-help-for-older-people-after-a-move-uk/">settling-in guide</a> covers the first weeks.
- q: Do you give care or medical advice?
  a: No. If you are worried about how someone is coping after a move, talk to their GP or your local council&rsquo;s adult social care team.
- q: How much does it cost?
  a: Packages start at {bronze}. Unpacking starts with Silver Comfort at {silver}. A Discovery Consultation costs {discovery}. The final price depends on the size of the home and is confirmed in writing before you book.
- q: Is the removal insured?
  a: Yes. Every Chayce removal is fully insured against loss or damage in transit, and the cover is set out in your service agreement before the move begins.
- q: Do you work outside Northampton?
  a: Yes. We are based in Northampton and arrange moves across the whole UK.
